  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Approximating the value of a definite integral</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Evaluate the integral:</p>
<p>\( \displaystyle \int_{@a@}^{@b@} {@func@} \, dx=\)&nbsp;<span style="font-size: 0.9375rem;">[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]&nbsp;[[feedback:prt1]]</span></p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b><h3>Worked solution</h3></b></p>
<p>To find the definite integral of \(\displaystyle f(x) = {@func@}\) from \(a = {@a@}\) to \(b = {@b@}\) , we can use the definite integral formula:</p>

<p>\( \displaystyle \int_{a}^{b} f(x)\, dx= F(b) - F(a)\), where \(F(x)\) is the antiderivative of \(f(x)\). </p>

<p>Let's find the antiderivative of \( \displaystyle f(x) = {@func@}\):</p>
<p>\( \displaystyle \int {@func@} \, dx= {@expr1@}\)</p>

<p>Now we can evaluate the definite integral from \(a = {@a@}\) to \(b = {@b@}\):</p>
<p>\( \begin{align} \displaystyle \int_{@a@}^{@b@}{@func@} \, dx &= \left[{@expr1@}\right]_{@a@}^{@b@}\\
                 & = {@fb@}-{@fa@} \\
                  &= {@expr2@}
 \end{align}\)</p>

<p>Therefore,</p>
<p>\( \displaystyle \int_{@a@}^{@b@} {@func@} \, dx={@ta@}\).</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
